# LeakSanitizer suppressions
# Suppresses known false-positive leak reports from third-party libraries.
# Loaded via: LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=$PWD/suppressions/lsan.supp
#
# Format: leak:<pattern>
# Pattern is matched against function name, source file, or binary file name
# in the symbolized stack trace of the leak report.
# Use ^ and $ to anchor to start/end of string.
#
# IMPORTANT: Only add entries here after confirming the leak is a known
# false positive (e.g., static caches freed at process exit).

# spdlog — small static pattern caches not freed at exit
leak:spdlog

# xxHash — constant global lookup tables
leak:XXH*

# mimalloc — internal per-thread caches (freed on thread exit, not process exit)
leak:mi_

# GoogleTest — static test registration records
leak:testing::

# Google Benchmark — static benchmark registration records
leak:benchmark::
